{"name":"Instant","hex":"#d9cec7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"instant","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very short period of time; a moment.","A single, usually precise, point in time."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Impending; imminent.","Urgent; pressing; acute."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Instant","blocks":[{"text":"In physics and the philosophy of science, instant refers to an infinitesimal interval in time, whose passage is instantaneous. In ordinary speech, an instant has been defined as \"a point or very short space of time,\" a notion deriving from its etymological source, the Latin verb instare, from in- + stare, meaning 'to stand upon or near.'"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant","wikidata":"Q16963779"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"instant":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/En-us-instant.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/20/En-us-instant.ogg/En-us-instant.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.765},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.623125},{"title":"Production of instant noodles","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Production_of_instant_noodles.jpg/500px-Production_of_inst